# Export Rules

## Browser API Strategy
- Primary: File System Access API (showDirectoryPicker) — lets user pick a folder and write files directly. Chrome/Edge only.
- Fallback: JSZip — bundle all files into a .zip and trigger download. For Firefox, Safari, and any browser without showDirectoryPicker.
- Use the browser-fs-access library to handle detection and fallback gracefully.
- Always feature-detect. Never assume showDirectoryPicker exists.

## Export Folder Structure
When exporting a song, create this structure:

```
/SongTitle/
  /audio/
    [sectionIntent]-[role]-[source]-[###].[ext]    (e.g., verse-bassline-audio-recording-001.wav)
  /midi/
    [sectionIntent]-[role]-[source]-[###].mid      (e.g., intro-chords-step-input-001.mid)
  /images/
    [original-filename].[ext]             (e.g., amp-settings-001.jpg)
  /notes/
    production-journal.md
    lyrics.txt
```

## Naming Conventions for Exported Files
- Use the idea's sectionIntent and role for the filename prefix.
- If sectionIntent is null/unassigned, use "unassigned" as prefix.
- Zero-pad the counter to 3 digits (001, 002, ...).
- Sanitize the song title for filesystem safety (no slashes, colons, special chars).
- Lowercase filenames.

## Export Content
- Audio: export the raw blob from IdeaMedia.
- MIDI: export the .mid blob from IdeaMedia. If only noteData exists (from note picker), serialize to .mid via @tonejs/midi first.
- Images: export the raw blob from IdeaMedia.
- Lyrics: combine song-level lyrics + section-level lyrics into a single .txt file, organized by section.
- Production Journal: combine all SongJournalEntry records into a single .md file, organized by topic. Strip HTML to markdown (or export as HTML with .html extension).

## Export Dialog
- Show a summary: X audio files, Y MIDI files, Z images.
- Preview the folder structure.
- Checkboxes for what to include (Audio, MIDI, Images, Lyrics, Journal).
- Two buttons: "Save to Folder" (File System Access) and "Download as ZIP" (JSZip).
- If File System Access is not available, only show the ZIP option.
